face-image: img/portraits/Joseph_Hawkins.jpg

With our grassroots connections, we have been able to influence the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] delegates to support Cormac Hawkins as the new [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] chairman. He has long been a friend of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and will be more inclined to collaborate with us compared to Renck. He also increases the appeal of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to the working class, though it comes at the cost of deepening the social and economic divisions once held together by religion.

