Adam Sedgewick has been elected as the chairman of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Vael, despite his Free Guild background, and will preside over a [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] less inclined to compromise with the left. He views the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] as a prototype for a <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>, <span style="color: #586593;">democratic</span>, <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth</span>, and <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> party, and aims to transform it according to the principles laid out in his proposed "Essen program" eight years prior. 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s middle class wing are in uproar over the vote, despite Sedgewick conceding his leadership of the Assembly delegation and the Minister-Presidency to his protege Edmund Askew. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": His election also attracts some dissenting <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> dissidents and guild-masters, who may result in a shift of the party towards the right. ?]